# PART 2: REDESIGN THE PAYMENT REVIEW MODAL

This is a very important part of the change.

Whenever a customer clicks Review & Pay, they must see an attractive, professional and properly structured modal explaining exactly what they are about to purchase or pay for.

The modal should not simply display a payment-method selector and an amount.

It should serve as a final transaction confirmation and policy-acceptance interface.

## 1. Modal structure

Use a premium institutional financial-interface design consistent with Jaystarbliss Studios branding.

Suggested hierarchy:

### A. Header

Title:

**Review Your Payment**

Supporting text:

Please review the payment details below before proceeding to secure checkout.

Include a clear close button.

### B. Payment description

Dynamically identify exactly what the customer is paying for.

Depending on the payment type, display:

- School or institution name.
- Student or learner name.
- Parent or payer name where applicable.
- Programme or curriculum track.
- Selected sub-programmes.
- Assigned tutor where relevant.
- Tuition period or billing cycle.
- Teaching delivery mode.
- Invoice or payment description.

For multi-child payments, clearly identify each child and the programmes selected for each child.

For school subscriptions, identify the institutional subscription and the selected programme tracks.

For individual learners, identify the actual learner and selected programme.

Do not show irrelevant or empty fields.

### C. Itemized financial breakdown

Present a clear financial summary.

Where applicable, include:

| Description | Amount |
|---|---:|
| Programme / Tuition Subtotal | ₦XX,XXX |
| Processing Fee | ₦X,XXX |
| Outstanding Balance | ₦X,XXX |
| Total Payable | ₦XX,XXX |

Only display applicable rows.

Make the final payable amount visually prominent.

For installment payments, clearly identify:

- Full contract or programme fee.
- Current installment percentage.
- Amount currently being paid.
- Remaining balance.

### D. Paystack explanation

Add a concise payment-provider notice:

"Your payment will be processed securely through Paystack. You will be redirected to Paystack's hosted checkout, where you can select an available payment method."

Do not list Card, Bank Transfer, OPay or Mobile Money as selectable options in our modal.

### E. Payment Policy acceptance

This section is mandatory.

Include a clearly identifiable section titled:

**PAYMENT POLICY — NO REFUNDS**

Display the following policy statement:

"No refund of fees paid to the other party will be made after payment has been successfully completed."

The wording must be clearly visible and readable.

Directly below it, display a small, unchecked checkbox:

**I have read and agree to the Payment Policy.**

The checkbox must:

- Be unchecked by default.
- Require an explicit customer action.
- Be accessible and properly labelled.
- Retain its checked state while the customer completes the current review.
- Reset appropriately when a different payment is being prepared.

The customer must not be able to proceed to payment without checking this box.

### F. Final payment action

The primary button should say:

**Pay through Paystack**

Do not include a payment-channel name in the button.

The button must remain disabled until the customer accepts the Payment Policy.

Display a helpful explanation when the checkbox has not been selected.

When the customer clicks the button:

- Validate the consent.
- Validate the selected payment details.
- Prevent accidental duplicate submissions.
- Initialize the transaction through our authenticated backend.
- Redirect to the returned Paystack authorization URL.

Display an appropriate loading state while the transaction is being initialized.

Provide a secondary Cancel or Go Back action.

